    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0684" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.515/76: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-07T15:00:00+03:06">January 7, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:51 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. The second 2 million riyals minted in England mentioned in Department’s 113,
                    December 20, 10 p.m.,<anchor n="39" xml:id="d729-f1"/> arrived here January 5,
                    and were delivered to Finance Minister<anchor n="40" xml:id="d729-f2"/> against
                    temporary receipt. Preparation of final receipts awaits Treasury certification
                    of quantity of silver used. Legation already has such certification from London
                    and Bombay mints.</p>
                <p>Responsible officials indicate that further quantities of Lend-Lease silver will
                    be requested in 1944 but that accurate determination of requirements awaits
                    agreement between local and British authorities about disposition of pilgrimage
                    “tariff items” now on deposit in sterling funds outside Saudi Arabia. See also
                    my 5, January 7, 2 p.m.</p>
                <p>Any developments will be promptly reported.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
